<title>CYPRUS: Doctors in Cyprus go on 48-hour strike.</title>
<headline>Doctors in Cyprus go on 48-hour strike.</headline>
<dateline>NICOSIA 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Some 400 doctors seeking pay rises and better pension benefits started a 48-hour strike in state-run hospitals in Cyprus on Thursday, their union said.</p>
<p>&quot;The strike has started,&quot; Glafcos Hadjipetrou, chairman of the civil servants union Pasydy, told Reuters.</p>
<p>A standby staff was on call to deal with emergency cases and in-patients. Other cases would be referred to the private sector, Hadjipetrou said.</p>
<p>He said government officials had ignored union requests for meetings to discuss the doctors' demands.</p>
<p>Health Minister Manolis Christofides has accused the doctors of abusing their right to strike.</p>
</text>
